{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-35520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-35520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of circles centered at the origin. Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/413a11a52ed6a4fc76c2848867d664a63fce24dd39088cdd5826b576d8e7b09c.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-35520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13f2862e4c559e910c05d0434297648f0136211c5d2ee539c3943f573afecf1a"} {"question" "q-35520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-35520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/22ff469fae1e93c0d805e7443c110c8c56b4f005b0ce2f4a641f19a23dfa3135.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/7c4530dc74747fc0bdae0ca4c8608a72dbf03ca413d4479c8a4b9224246ac01f.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/ae78f21487e5883b278f0b62a92b2b44ffe8e83e9bd942cf6c94ed4c46d18c67.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/b4642ea9b585ac066f2ed904b1bee4df7d1ff3449ba2d09afca8364b58f1dcba.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/e49f976cd92eac7780062c7013a29e6acb737d4496a1b61955d7c2ceac96084a.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-35520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/7c4530dc74747fc0bdae0ca4c8608a72dbf03ca413d4479c8a4b9224246ac01f.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-35527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=xy$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=-1$ gives a parabola\n- $c=0$ gives the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-35527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=\\pm 1$ then the level curves are $xy=\\pm 1,$ which are hyperbolas.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curves are $xy=0,$ which consists of the axes $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\nSo, only statements I and III are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-35527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13f2862e4c559e910c05d0434297648f0136211c5d2ee539c3943f573afecf1a"} {"question" "q-35527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-35527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-35527" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-71395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=1$ gives a line\n- $c=2$ gives a hyperbola\n- $c=0$ gives two lines" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-71395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=1,$ which is not a line.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=4,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}},$ which consists of two lines.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-71395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13f2862e4c559e910c05d0434297648f0136211c5d2ee539c3943f573afecf1a"} {"question" "q-71395" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-71395" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-71395" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-129117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/037422e7b1ce3b3d9067aba39c4fa85c6311770e63e70758c34aa61629c7f58e.png)\n\nWhich of the following could represent the level curves of the surface $z=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-129117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[-1,1].$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\in [-1,1].$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =c \\\\ y & =-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ can be any integer. \n\nNotice that the equations $y=-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡c+2\\pi n$ do not depend on $x.$ So, for a given $c\\in [-1,1]$ and integer $n$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of horizontal lines, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-129117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13f2862e4c559e910c05d0434297648f0136211c5d2ee539c3943f573afecf1a"} {"question" "q-129117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-129117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/09f1a18e1a6fdcd29a40026cbffd8e8bdec23511bb692a1e920c18f942042470.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/56e923e4c1e2603c9bd3c621df0a5a4043fcc6a37ac73427be14541407fc19d8.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/aa4d0cd189808c717648640c5543a632c099970a19d38d44298d409054f2627c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/bf0f4b592cde648f63b21523aba1a49aeeb3b4dcaf909ba72c4629e088ca372a.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-129117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/67e9cfee7779fdde389a0804e7f52372ca9434de56b6611d296d4ac9c0759f72.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-129118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=-x-y+2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-129118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nnotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider $c$-level curves for any real value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ -x-y+2 & =c \\\\ y & =-x+2-c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $-1.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/e20175ef9ac473a621a67d524e60cacc6e9a40ba30267fe81b4e6a093c780c28.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-129118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "13f2862e4c559e910c05d0434297648f0136211c5d2ee539c3943f573afecf1a"} {"question" "q-129118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/state.json" "file_sha256" "064d0b872e11eadbedccdc0d38dc3dd6d01e814e07b5a9d887bcdd17fdf30f67"} {"question" "q-129118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069946/assets/0162f31b5dbb35c6d370dff9b54257708df39b6957f6547059842cd31769669b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-worke